# Tracked worker self-heal / filter policy (config-under-management).
#
# Canonical, committed home for the worker-loop SELF-HEAL toggles that used to
# live only in a node's hand-deployed, git-UNTRACKED launcher
# (~/node1-worker-run.sh) — the exact file that silently froze the fleet for
# ~15h on 2026-09-08: a hand-edited FLEET_DOMAIN_FILTER=EFFECTIVE,CREDIBLE
# narrowed the worker to a domain with no pickable gaps, and because
# CHUMP_STARVE_AUTO_RELAX was never set there, the worker stood down 138x
# instead of auto-relaxing its filter. Nothing in git described the intended
# policy, so nothing could review it, reproduce it, or heal it.
#
# scripts/dispatch/worker.sh sources this file (guarded, best-effort) on every
# cycle from the auto-refreshed script-host checkout (RESILIENT-1080), so the
# policy reaches a live worker without hand-editing the per-node launcher.
# Values use ":=" assignment: an explicit value already set by the launcher or
# environment WINS (a node can still opt out), but an UNSET toggle — the drift
# state that caused the freeze — gets the fleet's intended default here.
#
# This file carries POLICY toggles only, never secret values and never node
# identity. The per-node launcher keeps setting node identity (AGENT_ID,
# WORKER_MACHINE, FLEET_SESSION, WORKER_SKILLS) and secret VALUES stay in the
# machine-local, gitignored ~/.chump/providers.env (RESILIENT-173: no secrets
# in git). To change the fleet's worker self-heal policy, edit THIS file and
# ship the PR — do not hand-edit a node's launcher, it will drift on the next
# fresh install / re-provision.

# INFRA-391 mode (a): auto-relax. When a worker has been starved for
# CHUMP_STARVE_THRESHOLD consecutive empty cycles, widen its own filter in
# place (drop FLEET_DOMAIN_FILTER -> bump effort tier -> bump priority tier,
# the smallest meaningful increase in blast radius each step) and reset the
# starve counter, instead of ramping toward the INFRA-613 stand-down that took
# the fleet dark. Default ON here so a narrow or drifted filter self-corrects.
# See docs/process/CAPABILITY_DECISIONS.md for the ON rationale + ratchet.
: "${CHUMP_STARVE_AUTO_RELAX:=1}"
export CHUMP_STARVE_AUTO_RELAX

# INFRA-391 mode (b): auto-shutdown. Mutually exclusive intent with auto-relax
# — exiting on starvation is the wrong default for an always-on owned node
# (the worker should stay ready and relax, not disappear until a human or the
# auto-restart daemon respawns it). Pinned OFF here so an inherited value
# cannot silently turn a starved worker into a dead one.
: "${CHUMP_STARVE_AUTO_SHUTDOWN:=0}"
export CHUMP_STARVE_AUTO_SHUTDOWN
